KNOWNBUG: [over.match.oper]/3.2 -- a reference-to-class lvalue operand (e.g.
`static_cast<std::ostream&>(x)`) does not participate in member operator@
overload resolution because CBMC's gate requires the operand's type node to be
exactly ID_struct_tag, not a reference to one.  So `ostream << <int>` inside a
member operator<< template body fails with "operator 'shl' not defined".  This is
the residual src/util (parse_options.cpp, typecheck.cpp) dog-food shl noise after
the free-vs-member-template fix.  A clean fix needs the combined member +
non-member candidate set of [over.match.oper]/3 for reference-typed operands.
Flip to CORE once that lands.
